<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Recôncavo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Recôncavo Baiano</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Recôncavo is the fertile coastal region surrounding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-all-saints">Bay of All Saints</a> in the Brazilian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahia">Bahia</a>. From the 16th century it was covered with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> plantations and tobacco farms worked by enslaved Africans, which made it one of the richest parts of colonial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. Towns such as Cachoeira and Santo Amaro keep a strong Afro-Brazilian culture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reconcavo.jpg" alt="Recôncavo" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: André Koehne · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baia_de_Todos_os_Santos.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
